ed $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.expansion_mrr_contribution, while churn exerted a drag of $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.churn_drag — making $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.dominant the dominant driver of the net shift."},{"op":"SECTION","text":"Plan-Level Breakdown"},{"op":"VIEW","component":"StreamChart","series":"plan_mrr_breakdown","text":"Net MRR by plan over time"},{"op":"EXPLAIN","refs":["segment_heterogeneity"],"anchor":"chart_plan_mrr_breakdown","text":"MRR levels differ significantly across Enterprise, Pro, and Starter plans ($finding:segment_heterogeneity.test, p = $finding:segment_heterogeneity.p_value), confirming that the aggregate trend masks meaningful variation by segment — the plan mix matters, not just the total."},{"op":"CAVEAT","refs":["grain_plan_month"],"anchor":"chart_plan_mrr_breakdown"},{"op":"INSIGHT","refs":["net_mrr_trend","net_mrr_change_decomposition","segment_heterogeneity"],"text":"The story across all three lenses is consistent: a genuine upward trend driven primarily by $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.dominant, concentrated unevenly across plans whose MRR levels are statistically distinct — meaning plan-mix shifts could amplify or dampen this trajectory going forward."},{"op":"METHOD","refs":["net_mrr_trend","net_mrr_split_comparison","net_mrr_change_decomposition","segment_heterogeneity"],"text":"Trends were estimated via OLS on monthly aggregates; the half-year contrast uses median net MRR over each span; the decomposition attributes the period-end change to each MRR component; plan heterogeneity was tested with one-way ANOVA or Kruskal-Wallis as declared."},{"op":"CONCLUSION","refs":["net_mrr_trend","net_mrr_current_state","net_mrr_split_comparison"],"text":"Net MRR rose $finding:net_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:net_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month, ending the year at $finding:net_mrr_current_state.latest_value and closing at $finding:net_mrr_current_state.pct_from_peak of the $finding:net_mrr_